{"id":"word:hebrew:H6419","type":"word","title":"פָּלַל","subtitle":"H6419 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to judge (officially or mentally); by extension, to intercede , pray","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to פָּלַל (H6419) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 84 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"פָּלַל (pâlal) means to judge (officially or mentally); by extension, to intercede , pray First listed occurrence: 1Chr 17 25."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"פָּלַל","transliteration":"pâlal","pronunciation":"paw-lal'","strong":"H6419","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6419","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["לְ/הִתְפַּלֵּ֖ל","וַ/יִּתְפַּלֵּ֥ל","וַ/יִּתְפַּלֵּ֨ל","מִתְפַּלֵּ֥ל","יִתְפַּלֵּ֣ל"],"morphs":[["HC/Vtw3ms",16],["HC/Vtq3cp",9],["HR/Vtc",8],["HVti3ms",5],["HVtrmsa",4],["HVtv2ms",4],["HC/Vtw1cs",4],["HVti3mp",3],["HVtj2ms",3],["HC/Vtv2ms",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to judge (officially or mentally); by extension, to intercede , pray","usage":"intreat, judge(-ment), (make) pray(-er, -ing), make supplication.","full":"H6419. palal [ מָּלַל ] 84 verb probably intervene, interpose (hence both arbitrate, judge , and intercede, pray , compare Dr 1Sam 2:25 ; Late Hebrew פלל (rare), נתפלל , pray , מִּילּוּל act of prayer , מְּלִילָה judicial matter ; — otherwise We Heid. (2), 126 who conjectures derivation for הִתְמַּלֵּל from Arabic notch edge (of sword, etc.), i.e. cut one-self in worship); — Pi`el mediate, judge: Perfect 3masculine singular consecutive, arbitrate , suffix וּפִלְלוֺ 1Sam 2:25 (but read probably 3 plural וּפִלְלוּ We Dr and others, word-play with ׳יִתְפ following); 2 feminine singular מִּלַּלְתְּ Ezek 16:52 mediate for ( ל person) namely, through thine own sins; 1 singular מִּלָּ֑לְתִּי Gen 48:11 (E; possibly denominative from פליל ) I did not judge (have the opinion, expect) to see, etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular וַיְפַלֵּל Psa 106:30 (absolute) he interposed (by slaying offender). Hithpa`el 80 Perfect 3masculine singular הִתְמַּלֵּל 1Kin 8:42 ; 1 singular הִתְמַּלָּ֑לְתִּי 1Sam 1:27 , etc.; Imperfect יִתְמַּלֵּל Psa 32:6 +; יִתְמַּלֶּלֿ 1Sam 2:25 ; 1 singular אֶתְאֶתְמּלָּ֑ל Psa 5:3 , etc.; Imperative הִתְמַּלֵּל Num 21:7 +, etc.; Infinitive construct הִתְמַּלֵּל Ezek 10:1 +, etc.; Participle מִתְמַּלֵּל Jer 42:4 +, etc.; — 1 specifically intercede (with ׳י ), with בעד , on behalf of Gen 20:7 ; Num 21:7 (E) Deut 9:20 ; 1Sam 12:23 6 t.; with לִ , 2:25 ; אֶליֿהוה Num 11:2 ; 21:7 (JE) Deut 9:26 ; with בעד + אליֿהוה 1Sam 7:5 ; Jer 29:7 4 t.; אלהֿאלהים Gen 20:17 (E); with על for 2Chr 30:18 ; Job 42:8 (late). 2 Generally pray , with אֶל , unto idol Isa 44:17 ; 45:20 ; unto Israel 45:14 ; להתפ אלמֿקדשׁ ׳בוֺא 16:12 . 3 pray (to ׳י ), absolute 1Kin 8:33 ; 2Kin 6:17 ; Ezra 10:1 ; Dan 9:20 ; 2Chr 6:24 ; 7:1 , 14 , with ׳אֶליֿ 1Sam 1:26 ; 8:6 ; 2Kin 4:33 ; 6:18 ; 20:2 = Isa 38:2 2Chr 32:24 , + 10 t.; ׳הִתְפ אֶליֿ ׳תפלה 2Sam 7:27 ; 1Kin 8:54 ; יהוה על 1Sam 1:10 (read אֶל ); לִפְנֵי 1:12 ; 1Kin 8:28 + 5t.; with לְ Dan 9:4 ; with אֶל of thing prayed for 1Sam 1:27 ; with אֶל against 2Kin 19:20 = Isa 37:21 (read עַל ); עַלזֹֿאת because of this 2Chr 32:20 ; Psa 32:6 ; with אֶל location: הַמָּקוֺם אֶלֿ 1Kin 8:29-30 , 35 2Chr 6:20-21 , 26 ; אֶלהַֿבַּית 1Kin 8:42 2Chr 6:32 ; with accusative הָעִיר דֶּרֶךְ 1Kin 8:44 2Chr 6:34 ; אַרְצָם דֶּרֶךְ 1Kin 8:48 2Chr 6:38 . 4 of poetical, liturgical prayer, absolute 1Sam 2:1 , with אֶל Jonah 2:2 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 17 25","keyReferences":["1Chr 17 25","1Kgs 8 28","1Kgs 8 29","1Kgs 8 30","1Kgs 8 33","1Kgs 8 35","1Kgs 8 42","1Kgs 8 44"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":84,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 17 25","book":"1Chr","chapter":17,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/הִתְפ